    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="d109-1" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10-12mSupp/d109-1"/>

                <head>110. Circular telegram 170 to certain American Republic posts, July 26<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d110-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1963-07-26T16:29:00">July 26, 1963, 4:29
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d110-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d110-1"/>
                <p>On assumption several other Hemisphere countries recognize Ecuadorean junta by
                    July 30–31 U.S. Government planning extend recognition July 31. You are
                    requested informally consult host govern<pb facs="0449" n="274" type="typeset"
                        xml:id="pg274"/>ment re above timing and any developments their plans on
                    recognition. Action posts other than BA, Santiago and Rio may also say U.S.
                    understands Argentina, Chile and Brazil considering recognition by July 31.</p>
                <closer><signed corresp="#p_RD_1">Rusk</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d110-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d110-f1-content">
                <p>U.S. plan to recognize Ecuadorean junta by July 31 if several other Hemisphere
                    countries do so by then. Confidential. 1 p. Kennedy Library, National Security
                    Files, Countries Series, Ecuador, July to November, 1963.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
